Firstly, install the `technologies` module if you haven't done so already:
```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install nginx-extras
```
Once installed, you can update your Nginx configuration to include the following code:
```nginx
http {
    # ... existing configuration ...

    # Enable the technologies module
    lingering http_technologies;

    index index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;

    # Add a link to every post
    location ~ (.*)\.html$ {
        # Fetch the post ID from the URL
        set $post_id $1;

        # Load the post metadata (you may need to adjust this path)
        proxy_pass http://localhost:5000/posts/$post_id;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;

        # Modify the HTML to include a link to the post
        types {

            # Before serving the HTML, load the post metadata and inject the link
            before_content http_technologies {

                # Load the post metadata (you may need to adjust this path)
                set $json '/path/to/post/meta/$post_id.json';

                # Load the metadata
                proxy_pass http://localhost:5000/post_meta/$post_id;
                proxy_set_header Host $host;
                proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
                proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;

                # Get the post title and permalink
                json_var title $json 'title';
                json_var permalink $json 'permalink';

                # Create the link
                response_var link "Post: <a href=\"$permalink\">$title</a>";
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This configuration uses the `http_technologies` module to inject a link into the HTML of each page. It fetches the post ID from the URL, loads the post metadata, and extracts the post title and permalink. Then, it creates a link using the post title and permalink.

Make sure to adjust the `proxy_pass` directives to point to your backend server where you're storing the post metadata.

Once you've applied these changes, restart your Nginx server and test your website to ensure the link is being injected correctly.

